  "_comment": "Entity-type classification for every real (non-VectorDB helper-function) table in the Table Builder catalog (https://ir-reports.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/dbcatalog/index.json). Built by inspecting each table's own columns, not its catalog summary text (a couple of summaries are copy-pasted/wrong — see notes). Purpose: given the table a selected metric resolves to (metric-registry.json's annual.prefer/quarterly.prefer, or the catalog's own table for non-registry metrics), look up table_entity_map[table] to know what kind of thing the Entity dropdown should let the user pick, and which column holds that entity's id/display name. is_entity_table:false rows are reference/metadata tables (a metric catalog or a JSON-key mapping) with no entity of their own to pick — they exist to be joined, not queried as a row-per-entity source. related_entity_* is set only for a table that joins two different entity types in one row (a holdings/relationship table) — entity_type/entity_id_column/entity_name_column always describe the table's OWN primary row identity.",
